# ============================================================
# Dr Manoj Clinic Automation — .gitignore
# CODE ONLY repo. Secrets and patient data must NEVER be committed.
# When in doubt, this file errs on the side of blocking.
# ============================================================

# ---- SECRETS: environment files ----
.env
.env.*
*.env
# (allow the safe templates only)
!*.env.example
!.env.example

# ---- SECRETS: keys / credentials (service-account JSON, tokens, certs) ----
# Block ALL .json by default so a key file can never slip in.
*.json
# allow only clearly-safe example/template json
!*.example.json
!dashboard/appsscript.json

# S203: signatures.json is the Marg REPORT SIGNATURE REGISTRY -- report types,
# title patterns and the end_marker that proves an export is complete. It holds
# no secrets (checked), and it is one of the files that existed ONLY on the two
# Windows PCs until S203. The blanket *.json rule above exists to keep
# credentials out; it was also silently excluding this. PUBLISH_ALL refused the
# whole push rather than drop it -- F-100's guard working exactly as intended.
!**/signatures.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-key.*
*credentials*
*secret*
*token*

# ---- CONTACT NUMBERS: F-185. Never in this repository, in any format. ----
# The PATIENT-DATA block below blocks .csv/.tsv/.xls/.xlsx and says nothing
# about .json. On 28-Aug a kit shipped 18 real supplier numbers in a .json
# inside deploy_kits and nothing would have stopped the next publish. Numbers
# live in the config store beside the archive, never here.
*phone*.json
*phones*
*contact*.json
*contacts*
*mobile*.json
_config/

# ---- PATIENT DATA: exports, mirrors, logs, recordings ----
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.jsonl
*.mp3
*.wav
*.vcf
wa_logs/
recordings/
exports/
uploads/
data/
data_backup_09_jun/
outputs/
Archive/


# ---- PYTHON runtime / build junk ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---- OS / editor noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# ---- Logs ----
*.log
recordings-archive/client_secret.json
recordings-archive/drive_token.json
recordings-archive/__pycache__/
!recordings-archive/get_drive_token.py

# ---- ATTENDANCE subsystem secrets (Session 59) ----
# att_config.py holds the attendance dashboard password + SECRET_KEY — NEVER commit.
# The non-secret attendance code (att_dashboard.py, att_core.py, attlistener_v2.py) IS committable.
att_config.py
attendance/att_config.py
console.db
console.db.tmp
transcript_cache.db
console_reviews.db
rec_cache/
*.tmp
attendance/staff_master.csv
# ---- Clinic Finance (S179) · PHI + money. MUST be in .gitignore BEFORE the
# ---- first commit of finance_app.py, not after (F-31 / F-49).
finance/finance.db
finance/finance.db-wal
finance/finance.db-shm
finance/finance.db.bak*
finance/scans/
finance/exports/
finance/access.log
finance/medical_legacy.csv
finance/medical_*.csv
finance/finance.db
finance/finance.db-wal
finance/finance.db-shm
finance/finance.db.bak*
finance/finance.db.pre*
finance/scans/
finance/exports/
finance/vendor/
finance/access.log
finance/backup.log
finance/medical_legacy.csv
finance/medical_*.csv
finance/upi_statements/
finance/marg_in/
finance/*_bills.csv
finance/*_items.csv
finance/REPORT_1.XLS
finance/REPORT_1.xls




# scratch: files staged for deletion via device bridge (device_bash cannot rm)
/_to_delete/
# S219: the per-session sweep folders only. Each carries a WHY_SAFE.txt
# naming every surviving copy; _to_delete_S219 alone is 3.8 MB of scratch.
# NOTE: timestamped canon backups (CANONICAL_MANIFEST.md.bak_S###) are NOT
# ignored -- this project commits them (the S203 one is tracked), and an
# ignore rule for them was added and removed at S219 after the publish gate
# refused: a file silently excluded is exactly what that gate exists to stop.
/_to_delete_S*/


# S218: the staff-cards registry is names+URLs only (no PHI, no secrets) and must publish
!deploy_kits/*/cards_registry.json

# S222: the per-person TILE GRANTS file, same shape and same reasoning -- logins and tile
# names only, no PHI, no secrets, no numbers. It is the file that took per-person tiles out
# of portal.py, so it has to ship with its kit or the kit installs nothing. Checked before
# this line was added: six logins, sixteen tile names, and the only digits in it are "2026".
!deploy_kits/*/tile_grants.json
# S223: F-300 RECURRED. `deploy_kits/S223_XRAY_LIST/` holds exactly one file --
# xray_list.json -- so the blanket *.json rule above made the ENTIRE KIT invisible
# to git. `git status` did not list it; nothing warned; it would have published as
# an empty folder. At S222 the publish gate caught this shape because other files
# in the kit were staged; here NOTHING was staged, so there was nothing to refuse.
# The rule: WHEN A KIT'S WHOLE PAYLOAD IS ONE .json, CHECK IT IS TRACKED BEFORE
# THE PUBLISH -- an ignored file is silent by design, and silence is the failure.
# This list carries the clinic's X-ray vocabulary only: study names, view codes,
# film sizes and misspellings. No patient, no number, no secret.
!deploy_kits/S223_XRAY_LIST/xray_list.json
